# Vulnerabilities this repository has decided not to act on, one per line.
#
# THE RULES FOR ADDING A LINE. An entry here silences a finding for everybody,
# forever, in a file nobody re-reads. So every entry must carry three things,
# and an entry without them should be deleted rather than researched:
#
#   1. the CVE id                 what is being silenced
#   2. why                        a sentence a reviewer can disagree with, not
#                                 "false positive" -- name the reason the code
#                                 is not reachable, or the risk is accepted
#   3. an expiry date             when somebody must look again
#
# Format:
#
#   # CVE-2025-00000  expires 2026-12-31
#   # Reached only by <thing this project does not do>. Re-check when <event>.
#   CVE-2025-00000
#
# WHAT DOES NOT BELONG HERE. The workflow already passes --ignore-unfixed, so a
# vulnerability with no released fix never reaches this file; adding one is
# silencing a finding that was never going to fail the build. And a CVE that is
# merely inconvenient to fix belongs in a dependency bump, not here.
#
# The file is currently EMPTY, and that is the intended steady state. If it
# stops being empty for long, the answer is usually an upgrade.
